    {
      "id": "claim_4864f2651a63474b99fec8c72fd87620",
      "statement": "MIGRATION.md defines five golden rules every migrated sheet must satisfy because of how the .gs code reads cells: header names are sacred (looked up via headers.indexOf, so a typo returns -1 and silently breaks), dates must be real Dates (instanceof Date, else treated as no date), numbers must be numbers (Withdrawal_Count 0/1/2/3, Current_Plan decimal), no stray whitespace in Allstars_ID/Work_Email or in headers, and Allstars_ID is the join key across Users/Enrollments/Beneficiaries/Audit_Log.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://MIGRATION.md#L9-L24",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:9c2d72caab7b20831ea71fc969b6eabad54e2bcad882603e9338697222ec0b68:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_33ffcd322cd64e34a2ed05b8ecfce4a1",
      "statement": "MIGRATION.md formalizes the lifecycle as 9 enrollment-cycle states (numbered 1-10, 6 the terminal lockout) plus a probation flag; states 1 and 7 are the only states with no Enrollments row, differing only in Users.Probation_End (future date blocks enrollment), and Withdrawal_Count holds steady through each enrollment and ticks up only on a withdrawal.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://MIGRATION.md#L50-L89",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:646e948e6f94ff99f24ed4c9dcd722b05bae5a962456265b556223fae48c96dc:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_cbd26798a3214949b0fdabce99e4c289",
      "statement": "Cooldown-versus-ready is decided purely by Last_Withdrawal_Date (+6 months vs today) with no separate flag, and an enrolled re-enrollment (states 5 and 10) must have Last_Withdrawal_Date >6 months ago because the app checks cooldown before enrolled-status, so a recent date would mis-display an enrolled member as Cooldown.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://MIGRATION.md#L115-L124",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:c56dec0f957995f8263bbfc00565ad6497ba70c7fd036ec5d7af1128bf848059:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
